---
title: KWin Window Manager
order: 2
description: KWin (X11/Wayland), window rules, shortcuts, compositing
tags: [kwin, window-manager, compositing, shortcuts, wayland, x11]
---

KWin is Plasma's window manager and compositor, available as kwin_x11 or kwin_wayland.

@text
KWin Process Management

@code bash
# Check which KWin is running
pgrep -a kwin

# Restart KWin (X11) — replaces running instance
kwin_x11 --replace &disown

# Restart KWin (Wayland) — replaces running instance
kwin_wayland --replace &disown

# Reconfigure KWin without restart (reload settings)
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure

@text
Compositing

Toggle and configure the compositor for effects, transparency, and vsync.

@code bash
# Check if compositing is active
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Compositor org.kde.kwin.Compositing.active

# Toggle compositing on/off
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Compositor suspend
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Compositor resume

# Keyboard shortcut: Alt+Shift+F12 toggles compositing by default

# Set compositing backend via config
kwriteconfig5 --file kwinrc --group Compositing --key Backend OpenGL
kwriteconfig5 --file kwinrc --group Compositing --key GLCore true

# Disable animations
kwriteconfig5 --file kwinrc --group Plugins --key kwin4_effect_fadeEnabled false
kwriteconfig5 --file kwinrc --group Plugins --key slidingpopupsEnabled false

# Force full recomposite pipeline
kwriteconfig5 --file kwinrc --group Compositing --key GLPreferBufferSwap a

@text
Window Rules

Window rules let you override behavior for specific applications (size, position, desktop, etc.).

@code bash
# Window rules are stored in ~/.config/kwinrulesrc
# Open the window rules editor
kcmshell5 kcm_kwinrules
# Plasma 6
kcmshell6 kcm_kwinrules

# Get window class for rule matching (click on target window)
xprop WM_CLASS

# Wayland alternative — use xprop substitute
xdotool getactivewindow getwindowname

# Example kwinrulesrc entry (added manually or via GUI):
# [1]
# Description=Float Dolphin
# wmclass=dolphin
# wmclassmatch=1
# above=true
# aboverule=2
# types=1

# Apply rules without restart
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure

@text
Keyboard Shortcuts

KWin shortcuts are stored in kglobalshortcutsrc and managed via D-Bus or the settings UI.

@code bash
# List all KWin global shortcuts
qdbus org.kde.kglobalaccel /component/kwin shortcutNames

# View a specific shortcut action
qdbus org.kde.kglobalaccel /component/kwin shortcut "Window Maximize"

# Open the keyboard shortcut settings module
kcmshell5 keys
# Plasma 6
kcmshell6 kcm_keys

# Useful default KWin shortcuts:
# Meta+Up           Maximize window
# Meta+Down         Minimize/restore
# Meta+Left/Right   Tile left/right
# Meta+PgUp/PgDn    Switch virtual desktop
# Alt+Tab           Window switcher
# Alt+F4            Close window
# Meta+D            Show desktop
# Ctrl+F8           Desktop grid (overview)
# Ctrl+F9           Present windows (all)
# Ctrl+F10          Present windows (current desktop)

@text
Window Operations via D-Bus

@code bash
# Get active window caption
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin org.kde.KWin.activeWindow

# List supported effects
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Effects org.kde.kwin.Effects.listOfEffects

# Check if a specific effect is loaded
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Effects org.kde.kwin.Effects.isEffectLoaded "slide"

# Load/unload an effect
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Effects org.kde.kwin.Effects.loadEffect "wobblywindows"
qdbus org.kde.KWin /Effects org.kde.kwin.Effects.unloadEffect "wobblywindows"

@text
KWin Scripting

KWin has a JavaScript scripting interface for window management automation.

@code bash
# Scripts stored in ~/.local/share/kwin/scripts/
# Install a KWin script
plasmapkg2 -t kwinscript -i /path/to/script.kwinscript

# List installed KWin scripts
plasmapkg2 -t kwinscript -l

# Enable/disable a KWin script via config
kwriteconfig5 --file kwinrc --group Plugins --key myscriptEnabled true
qdbus org.kde.KWin /KWin reconfigure

# Run a script once for testing
dbus-send --session --dest=org.kde.KWin \
  /Scripting org.kde.kwin.Scripting.loadScript \
  string:"/path/to/script.js" string:"test"
